IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`
IMPORT `cat-regulations-2012`
IMPORT `part-1-preliminary`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA), compilation 00-l0-01, currency start 25 Sep 2025 (mrdoc_48898).
-- Part 2 Division 2 -- Microchipping: ss 14-17. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01.
-- Offences arise by Interpretation Act s 72 from the penalty lines (REF-39); continuing
-- obligations by s 71 (REF-41); periods of days by s 61 (REF-40).

§ `Section 14 -- Cats to be microchipped`

-- s 14(2): "A cat is exempt from microchipping if a certificate given by a veterinarian stating
-- that the implantation of a microchip in the cat may adversely affect the health and welfare
-- of the cat applies in respect of the cat."
-- s 14(3): "A certificate referred to in subsection (2) cannot apply in respect of a cat that
-- is under 6 months of age."
-- FORK-13, reading A (taken): (3) is judged on the day in question. A certificate given while
-- the cat was under 6 months begins to apply when the cat reaches 6 months.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(2), (3) (FORK-13 reading A)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2) --` c `is exempt from microchipping on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `microchipping health certificate`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST cert THEN
            "a certificate given by a veterinarian" ... cert's `given by`'s `is a veterinarian`
        ... "stating that the implantation of a microchip ... may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat"
            ... cert's `states that the procedure may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat`
        ... `the day number of` (cert's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` t
        ... "(3) cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6 months of age"
            ... c `has reached 6 months of age on` t

-- FORK-13, reading B: (3) is judged when the certificate is given; one given while the cat was
-- under 6 months never applies.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(2), (3) (FORK-13 reading B)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2), reading B --` c `is exempt from microchipping on` t IF
    CONSIDER c's `microchipping health certificate`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST cert THEN
            cert's `given by`'s `is a veterinarian`
        AND cert's `states that the procedure may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat`
        AND `the day number of` (cert's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` t
        AND c `has reached 6 months of age on` (cert's `given on`)

-- s 14(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is
-- microchipped, unless the cat is exempt from microchipping. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- In operation from 1 November 2013 (s 2(c)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(1)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is microchipped applies to` o `for` c `on` t IF
        "The owner" ... `the person` o `is an owner of` c `on` t
    ... "of a cat that has reached 6 months of age" ... c `has reached 6 months of age on` t
    ... "unless the cat is exempt from microchipping" ... NOT `s 14(2) --` c `is exempt from microchipping on` t
    ... `the day number of` (`the date` 2013 11 1) AT MOST `the day number of` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(1)
GIVEN o IS A `Person`, c IS A `Cat`, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) --` o `contravenes the subsection for` c `on` t IF
        `s 14(1) -- the duty to ensure the cat is microchipped applies to` o `for` c `on` t
    ... "must ensure that the cat is microchipped" ... NOT `s 3(1) --` c `is microchipped on` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(1); Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(b)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 14(1) -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 14"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a subsection, but not at the foot of the section`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 14(1)"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 15 -- Microchip implanter to give information to microchip database company`

-- s 15: "A microchip implanter who implants a microchip in a cat must, within 7 days after the
-- microchip is implanted, give notice in writing in the form, if any, prescribed of the
-- information prescribed to the microchip database company for that cat.
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- No form is prescribed (REF-33); the information is Cat Regulations r 17.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15 -- the duty to notify applies to the implant in` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `implant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST i THEN
            "A microchip implanter" ... `s 3(1) -- is a microchip implanter` (i's `implanted by`)
        ... "who implants a microchip" ... `s 3(1) -- the device is a microchip` i
        ... "to the microchip database company for that cat" ... `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c

-- The last day for the notice: 7 days after the day of implanting, that day not counted (IA
-- s 61(1)(b)), moved to the next day that is not an excluded day (IA s 61(1)(e)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15; Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(b), (e)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`s 15 -- the last day for notice of the implant in` c `given the holidays` holidays MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `implant`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date` 1970 1 1
    WHEN JUST i THEN `s 61 -- the last day for a thing to be done within` 7 `days after` (i's `implanted on`) `given the holidays` holidays

-- A notice complies if it is in writing, to the company for the cat, and of every item r 17
-- prescribes.
GIVEN wanted IS A LIST OF `Information item`
      given IS A LIST OF `Information item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every item of` wanted `is among` given IF
    CONSIDER wanted
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN w FOLLOWED BY rest THEN w `is an item among` given AND `every item of` rest `is among` given

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15; Cat Regulations 2012 r 17
GIVEN n IS A `Notice`, c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15 -- the notice` n `is of the information prescribed, to the company for` c IF
        "in writing" ... n's `in writing`
    ... "to the microchip database company for that cat" ... n's `given to` EQUALS `the name of the microchip database company for` c
    ... "of the information prescribed" ... `every item of` `r 17 -- the information prescribed under s 15` `is among` (n's `items`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, notice IS A MAYBE `Notice`, t IS A `Calendar date`, holidays IS A LIST OF `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15 -- the implanter contravenes the section for` c `, the notice being` notice `, on` t `given the holidays` holidays IF
        `s 15 -- the duty to notify applies to the implant in` c
    ... `the day number of` (`s 15 -- the last day for notice of the implant in` c `given the holidays` holidays) LESS THAN `the day number of` t
    ... NOT `in time`
    WHERE
        `in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER notice
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST n THEN
                    `s 15 -- the notice` n `is of the information prescribed, to the company for` c
                AND `the day number of` (n's `given on`) AT MOST `the day number of` (`s 15 -- the last day for notice of the implant in` c `given the holidays` holidays)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 15 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 15"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 15"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 16 -- Microchip database company's obligations`

-- s 16: "A microchip database company for a cat must keep and maintain in its microchip
-- database the information prescribed under section 15 in respect of the cat.
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 16; Cat Regulations 2012 r 17
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, held IS A LIST OF `Information item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16 -- the company for` c `contravenes the section, holding` held IF
        "A microchip database company for a cat" ... `s 3(1) -- there is a microchip database company for` c
    ... "must keep and maintain ... the information prescribed under section 15"
        ... NOT `every item of` `r 17 -- the information prescribed under s 15` `is among` held

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 16; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 16 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 16"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 16"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Section 17 -- Interference with microchips`

-- s 17: "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, remove or interfere with a microchip
-- implanted in a cat. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 17
GIVEN `removes or interferes with a microchip implanted in a cat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 -- a person who` `removes or interferes with a microchip implanted in a cat` `, with excuse` `has a reasonable excuse` `, contravenes the section` IF
        "remove or interfere with a microchip implanted in a cat" ... `removes or interferes with a microchip implanted in a cat`
    ... "without reasonable excuse" ... NOT `has a reasonable excuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 17; Interpretation Act 1984 s 72(1)(a)
GIVETH A `Penalty line`
`s 17 -- penalty line` MEANS `Penalty line` WITH
    `in`                                       IS "Cat Act 2011 s 17"
    `placement`                                IS `at the foot of a section, without qualification`
    `the unit at whose foot it sits`           IS "s 17"
    `subsections it is expressed to apply to`  IS EMPTY
    `maximum fine`                             IS 5000
    `the contrary is expressly provided`       IS FALSE

§ `Interpretation Act s 71 -- which duties continue`

-- s 15 is a duty to do a thing within a period: s 71(1). s 14(1) and s 16 specify no period:
-- s 71(2) applies if they are duties "to do an act or thing" (FORK-12 reading A, taken).
-- s 17 is a prohibition, to which s 71 does not apply.
@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71 (FORK-12 reading A)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 15 is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing within a period or before a time`

@ref Interpretation Act 1984 s 71(2) (FORK-12 reading A)
GIVETH A `Kind of duty`
`s 71 -- s 14(1) is` MEANS `a duty to do a thing with no period or time specified`
